{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Rpga4rZfcEhyz4Qn9bSGmc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that re-implements Unix utilities in Go, deriving specs from C source code and verifying parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/` holds per-utility implementations, `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform-divergent syscalls, `pkg/format/` provides shared output formatting, and `magefiles/` exposes build targets.\n\n**Current state**: The implementation of `cmd/ts/main.go` exists. The differential testing harness (`pkg/testutils/difftest.go`, `normalize.go`) exists. PRDs, use cases, and test suites are written for all releases through rel02.1. **No differential test file exists for cmd/ts yet.**\n\n**Current release**: **rel01.0** (in_progress) — the only use case is `rel01.0-uc001-ts` (in_progress). The test suite `test-rel01.0` defines 12 test cases. The implementation exists but the test file `cmd/ts/ts_test.go` does not.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe earliest incomplete release is rel01.0. The implementation (`cmd/ts/main.go`) and harness (`pkg/testutils/`) are done. The missing deliverable is the differential test file that exercises all test cases from `test-rel01.0.yaml` and calls `RunDiffTests`. This is the single blocking item for completing rel01.0.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/ts differential tests -- prd004-ts R9, prd001-testutils R1-R3\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/ts/main.go (existing ts implementation to test)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (RunDiffTests API, DiffTest struct, FileExpectation)\n      - pkg/testutils/normalize.go (TimestampNormalizer, NormalizeFunc, ComposeNormalizers)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (all 12 test case definitions with inputs, normalization, expected outputs, and PRD traces)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-ts.yaml (R9 differential testing requirements)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (harness contract, AC1 usage pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ts/ts_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Differential tests for cmd/ts exercising all 12 test cases from test-rel01.0.yaml\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Set up test binary discovery in TestMain. Build the Go ts binary via\n          \"go build -o <tmpdir>/ts .\" and store the path in a package-level variable.\n          Locate the reference binary via exec.LookPath(\"ts\") (installed via\n          brew install moreutils). If either binary is unavailable, skip all tests\n          with t.Skip and a descriptive message. Per prd001-testutils AC1, the test\n          function defines a []DiffTest slice and calls RunDiffTests(t, goBinary,\n          refBinary, tests).\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement wall-clock timestamp test cases from test-rel01.0.yaml:\n          default_format_three_lines (stdin \"line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n\", no args),\n          default_format_empty_stdin (stdin \"\", no args),\n          default_format_partial_last_line (stdin \"partial\" with no trailing newline, no args),\n          custom_strftime_format (args [\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"], stdin \"hello\\nworld\\n\"),\n          and subsecond_format_dotS (args [\"%.S\"], stdin \"test\\n\").\n          All must apply TimestampNormalizer. Per prd004-ts R1.1-R1.6, R2.1-R2.4.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement elapsed-mode test cases from test-rel01.0.yaml:\n          elapsed_since_start_mode (args [\"-s\"], stdin \"a\\nb\\nc\\n\") and\n          incremental_mode (args [\"-i\"], stdin \"first\\nsecond\\nthird\\n\").\n          Both must apply TimestampNormalizer for elapsed HH:MM:SS prefixes.\n          Per prd004-ts R3.1-R3.2, R4.1-R4.2.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement monotonic_clock_mode test case from test-rel01.0.yaml:\n          args [\"-m\"], stdin \"tick\\n\". Apply TimestampNormalizer.\n          Per prd004-ts R5.1-R5.2.\n      - id: R5\n        text: |\n          Implement relative-mode test cases from test-rel01.0.yaml:\n          relative_mode_syslog_timestamp (args [\"-r\"], stdin \"Jan  1 00:00:00 boot message\\n\",\n          apply TimestampNormalizer to replace relative age string) and\n          relative_mode_no_timestamp_passthrough (args [\"-r\"],\n          stdin \"no timestamp here\\n\", no normalization needed).\n          Per prd004-ts R6.1-R6.4.\n      - id: R6\n        text: |\n          Implement error and mutual-exclusivity test cases from test-rel01.0.yaml:\n          incremental_and_elapsed_mutually_exclusive (args [\"-i\", \"-s\"], stdin \"\",\n          expected non-zero exit, stderr contains \"usage\") and\n          invalid_flag (args [\"-z\"], stdin \"\", expected non-zero exit,\n          stderr contains \"usage\"). No normalization. Per prd004-ts R3.4, R7.2.\n      - id: R7\n        text: |\n          Implement tz_environment_respected test case from test-rel01.0.yaml:\n          args [\"%H:%M:%S\"], stdin \"event\\n\", env includes \"TZ=UTC\".\n          Apply TimestampNormalizer. Per prd004-ts R8.1.\n      - id: R8\n        text: |\n          Apply TimestampNormalizer from pkg/testutils to all DiffTest entries whose\n          output contains non-deterministic wall-clock or elapsed timestamps, using the\n          Normalize field ([]NormalizeFunc). This is required by prd004-ts R9.1 to\n          ensure differential tests pass despite wall-clock differences between the Go\n          binary and the reference binary.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Per prd001-testutils AC1, the test function defines a []DiffTest slice and calls\n          RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) from a standard TestXxx function.\n          The DiffTest struct is imported from pkg/testutils with fields Name, Args, Stdin,\n          Env, Normalize, Timeout, and WorkDir per prd001-testutils R1.1-R1.4.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Per test-rel01.0.yaml preconditions, all test cases set LC_ALL=C in the DiffTest.Env\n          field. Wall-clock tests also set a fixed TZ (e.g., TZ=America/New_York) to ensure\n          consistent strftime output. The tz_environment_respected test overrides with TZ=UTC.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Per prd001-testutils R4.2 and AC3, TimestampNormalizer replaces strftime-formatted\n          timestamps with the fixed placeholder \"TIMESTAMP\". It is passed in the\n          DiffTest.Normalize slice ([]NormalizeFunc) per prd001-testutils R4.3. For tests\n          with no non-deterministic output (invalid_flag, relative_mode_no_timestamp_passthrough),\n          Normalize is nil.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Build the Go binary in TestMain using exec.Command(\"go\", \"build\", \"-o\", path, \".\")\n          to avoid requiring mage build to have been run. Use os.MkdirTemp for the binary\n          output directory. Store goBinary and refBinary paths in package-level variables.\n          Call os.Exit(m.Run()) at the end of TestMain.\n      - id: D5\n        text: |\n          Per prd001-testutils R3.6, each DiffTest.Name must match the test case name from\n          test-rel01.0.yaml (e.g., \"default_format_three_lines\", \"elapsed_since_start_mode\")\n          so individual failures are identifiable in go test output via t.Run.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: |\n          go test ./cmd/ts/... passes with no failures when both ./bin/ts (or freshly built\n          binary) and reference ts (brew install moreutils) are available.\n      - id: AC2\n        text: |\n          All 12 test cases from test-rel01.0.yaml are represented as DiffTest entries:\n          default_format_three_lines, default_format_empty_stdin, default_format_partial_last_line,\n          custom_strftime_format, subsecond_format_dotS, elapsed_since_start_mode,\n          incremental_mode, incremental_and_elapsed_mutually_exclusive, monotonic_clock_mode,\n          relative_mode_syslog_timestamp, relative_mode_no_timestamp_passthrough, invalid_flag.\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          TimestampNormalizer is applied to all DiffTest entries with non-deterministic output\n          (wall-clock and elapsed timestamps). Tests without timestamps (invalid_flag,\n          relative_mode_no_timestamp_passthrough) have nil Normalize.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          All DiffTest entries include LC_ALL=C in the Env field per test-rel01.0 preconditions.\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          Tests skip gracefully with t.Skip when either the Go binary cannot be built or the\n          reference ts binary is not found on PATH.\n      - id: AC6\n        text: cmd/ts/ts_test.go compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82530,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82530},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d6836f6-1af5-4b60-ac6a-0bfc8a249753","uuid":"51048f54-feca-428c-bc2b-4175adf17da8"}
